  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kaashif Youth Livelihoods Project in Mogadishu and Jowhar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Youth skills training and job placement. Beneficiaries: 200 youth, of whom 100 are women. Summary: This project will provide marketable skills training for 200 youth in Mogadishu (Dharkenley, Hodan and Waberi districts) and Middle Shabelle (Jowhar district) over two years. Beneficiaries will be trained in: secretarial and computer skills; electricity; mobile phone repair; carpentry, auto-mechanics; beauty and hairdressing. Trainees will also engage in business and job placements to acquire experience and get employed to improve their livelihoods.</narrative>
  </description>
